course: dictionary
lesson: 10171
title: One word, many meanings: tickle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word tickle has more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. When someone tickles you, they touch you lightly, often on the ribs or feet, so that you laugh and wriggle. «The feather tickled my nose» means the feather gave my nose a light, itchy feeling.
explain: Tickle can also mean to amuse someone. «The joke tickled me» does not mean anyone touched you. It means the joke made you laugh or smile. Check the clues: is anything touching anyone, or is something funny happening?
explain: Tickling in play is fun for many families, but it must always stop when someone says stop. Body safety lessons teach that you have a right to say no to tickling, even from family, and others should respect that. Feeling happy in a game is not the same as wanting it to carry on.
fact: Tickle can be a verb: to tickle, tickles, tickled, tickling.
fact: Tickle can also be a noun: «a tickle in my throat» or «a light tickle on my arm».
fact: «Tickled pink» means very pleased, and it does not mean anything about paint.
fact: You cannot tickle yourself, because your brain expects your own touch and does not treat it as a surprise.
fact: People have a right to say no to tickling, and others should respect it, even in play.
exercise: «The feather tickled my nose.» What does tickled mean here? | Made it go numb | *It gave my nose a light, itchy feeling | Hurt badly | Painted it pink
exercise: «The joke tickled me.» What does tickled mean here? | *It made me laugh or feel amused | It made me angry | It made me tired | It made me cry
exercise: «The cat pats his cheek and tickles him with his tail, and the baby laughs.» Why does the baby laugh? | A cold bath surprised him | Loud music is playing | He was told off | *The cat's tail is tickling him
test: «I felt a tickle on my arm.» In this sentence, what is a tickle? | A type of fruit | A loud noise | *A light touch or itchy feeling | A kind of big, hard hug
test: Lily says she is «tickled pink» about her swimming medal. What does she mean? | Her medal is painted pink | *She is very pleased | She is bored of swimming | She is very cold
exam: Sam is playing a tickle game, says «stop», but his uncle keeps going. What should Sam do? | Tickle his uncle back until he stops | Hide under the table and wait for the game to end | *Say stop clearly again and tell a trusted adult | Keep laughing and say nothing
